                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1-\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos^2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}&=\\frac{(1+\\sin\\theta)^2}{1-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}&=\\frac{(1+\\sin\\theta)^2}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}&=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)^2\\\\\\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{1-\\sin\\theta}&=(\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThus RHS equals LHS.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
