          },
          "worked": "For $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$, the known identity gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta)(\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta)&=\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan^2\\theta=1.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta=\\frac{1}{(\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta)}$, and\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sec\\theta(\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta)-1&=\\frac{2\\sec\\theta}{\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta}-1\\\\2\\sec\\theta(\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta)-1&=\\frac{2\\sec\\theta-(\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta)}{\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta}\\\\2\\sec\\theta(\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta)-1&=\\frac{\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta}{\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta}\\\\2\\sec\\theta(\\sec\\theta-\\tan\\theta)-1&=\\frac{1-\\sin\\theta}{1+\\sin\\theta}.\\end{align*}$$\nThus LHS equals RHS.",
