          "worked": "For $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, use the preceding identity to replace the second fraction.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1+\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1+\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1+\\cos\\theta}&=2\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nThus LHS equals RHS.",
