          "worked": "For $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{1+\\cot^2\\theta}&=\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{1+\\cot^2\\theta}&=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{1+\\cot^2\\theta}&=\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nAlso,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}&=\\frac{\\tan\\theta}{\\sec^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\cos^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}&=\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth equalities hold on the common domain.",
